# Component Template: {ComponentName}

Copy this template and replace `{ComponentName}` with your actual component name.

---

```tsx
// src/components/{ComponentName}/{ComponentName}.tsx
import { forwardRef, memo } from 'react'
import { cn } from '@/lib/utils'
import type { {ComponentName}Props } from './types'

/**
 * {ComponentName} - [Brief description of what this component does]
 *
 * @example
 * ```tsx
 * <{ComponentName} variant="primary" />
 * ```
 */
export const {ComponentName} = memo(forwardRef<HTMLDivElement, {ComponentName}Props>(
  function {ComponentName}(
    {
      variant = 'default',
      size = 'md',
      className,
      children,
      ...props
    },
    ref
  ) {
    return (
      <div
        ref={ref}
        className={cn(
          // Base styles
          'relative inline-flex items-center justify-center',
          // Variant styles
          variant === 'default' && 'bg-background text-foreground',
          variant === 'primary' && 'bg-primary text-primary-foreground',
          variant === 'secondary' && 'bg-secondary text-secondary-foreground',
          // Size styles
          size === 'sm' && 'h-8 px-3 text-sm',
          size === 'md' && 'h-10 px-4 text-base',
          size === 'lg' && 'h-12 px-6 text-lg',
          // Custom className
          className
        )}
        {...props}
      >
        {children}
      </div>
    )
  }
))

// Display name for React DevTools
{ComponentName}.displayName = '{ComponentName}'
```

---

## Usage Notes

### When to use `memo()`
- Component receives primitive props (strings, numbers, booleans)
- Component is pure (same props = same output)
- Component renders frequently in lists or parent re-renders

### When NOT to use `memo()`
- Component has internal state that changes often
- Props are complex objects that change reference often
- Component is lightweight and memo overhead isn't worth it

### `forwardRef` Pattern
Always use `forwardRef` when:
- Parents may need to access the DOM element
- Component wraps native elements
- Component is used in form libraries (react-hook-form, etc.)

---

## Customization Points

Replace these placeholders:
- `{ComponentName}` - Your component name (PascalCase)
- `HTMLDivElement` - Change if wrapping different element (e.g., `HTMLButtonElement`)
- Variant options - Customize to your design system
- Size options - Adjust to your spacing scale
- Base styles - Match your project's design patterns
